#ASSERT `s 171F(4) the pre-commencement period` EQUALS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 11 5 1987, `the last day` IS Date 8 10 1989
#ASSERT `s 171F(4) the person is treated as having been incapable of work on the day` (Date 11 5 1987) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171F(4) the person is treated as having been incapable of work on the day` (Date 8 10 1989) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171F(4) the person is treated as having been incapable of work on the day` (Date 10 5 1987) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171F(4) the person is treated as having been incapable of work on the day` (Date 9 10 1989) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171F(4) the person is treated as having been incapable of work on the day` (Date 1 1 1988) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171F(4) the person is treated as having been incapable of work on the day` (Date 1 1 1988) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 171G supplementary provisions`

-- (1) the Part does not apply for Part V, Part XI or a prescribed purpose; any other purpose is for s 171A(1)
#ASSERT `s 171G(1) this Part applies for the purpose` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171G(1) this Part applies for the purpose` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171G(1) this Part applies for the purpose` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171G(1) this Part applies for the purpose` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) "prescribed" means specified in or determined in accordance with regulations
#ASSERT `s 171G(2) the matter is prescribed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171G(2) the matter is prescribed` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) a week is any period of 7 days, both ends counted
#ASSERT `s 171G(2) the period is a week` (`s 171B test period` 0 6) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171G(2) the period is a week` (`s 171B test period` 0 5) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171G(2) the period is a week` (`s 171B test period` 0 7) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171G(2) the week convention` EQUALS `any period of 7 days`

§§ `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work, the whole Part`

-- arguments: s 171G(1) result, s 171A(1) result, s 171A(2) result, s 171A(3) result, s 171E(1) result, s 171D(1) result,
-- the test that decides, the own occupation test result, the personal capability assessment result
-- the own occupation test decides, and the person is incapable on it
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING `s 171D(1) no treatment under this subsection applies` `s 171C(1) the own occupation test` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the own occupation test decides, and the person is not incapable on it
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING `s 171D(1) no treatment under this subsection applies` `s 171C(1) the own occupation test` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a personal capability assessment decides: its outcome is the answer (incapable, capable, or not carried out)
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING `s 171D(1) no treatment under this subsection applies` `s 171C(1) a personal capability assessment` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING `s 171D(1) no treatment under this subsection applies` `s 171C(1) a personal capability assessment` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING `s 171D(1) no treatment under this subsection applies` `s 171C(1) a personal capability assessment` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- the 197th day: the text does not say which test decides
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING `s 171D(1) no treatment under this subsection applies` `s 171C(1) the text does not say which test decides` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the Part does not apply for the purpose (s 171G(1)): not covered here
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING `s 171D(1) no treatment under this subsection applies` `s 171C(1) the own occupation test` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- another provision expressly provides otherwise (s 171A(1)): not covered here
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING `s 171D(1) no treatment under this subsection applies` `s 171C(1) the own occupation test` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- regulations treat the person as capable of work (s 171A(2), s 171A(3) or s 171E(1)): capable, whatever the test says
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING `s 171D(1) no treatment under this subsection applies` `s 171C(1) the own occupation test` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `s 171D(1) no treatment under this subsection applies` `s 171C(1) the own occupation test` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) `s 171D(1) no treatment under this subsection applies` `s 171C(1) the own occupation test` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a regulation that does not bite (JUST FALSE) changes nothing
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) `s 171D(1) no treatment under this subsection applies` `s 171C(1) the own occupation test` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 171D(1): treated as incapable or as capable, whatever the test says
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING `s 171D(1) treated as incapable of work` `s 171C(1) the own occupation test` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING `s 171D(1) treated as capable of work` `s 171C(1) the own occupation test` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- opposite treatments: the text does not say which prevails
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING `s 171D(1) treated as incapable of work` `s 171C(1) the own occupation test` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- regulations under s 171D(1) give both treatments: the text does not say which prevails, whatever the test says
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING `s 171D(1) regulations give both treatments` `s 171C(1) the own occupation test` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 171D(1) treats the person as capable and so does s 171A(2): capable
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING `s 171D(1) treated as capable of work` `s 171C(1) the own occupation test` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 171D(1) treats the person as incapable and a regulation under s 171A(2) that does not bite (JUST FALSE) is no treatment: incapable
#ASSERT `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING NOTHING `s 171D(1) treated as incapable of work` `s 171C(1) the own occupation test` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
